  "description": "Mooncake memory pressure and SSD offload diagnostics. Compares allocation growth, completed memory eviction, logical file-storage growth, optional client SSD metrics, and allocation failures.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "liveNow": false,
  "panels": [
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "How to read this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "## Mooncake memory / SSD offload diagnosis\n\n- **Estimated memory ingress** = net memory growth + completed memory eviction. It is an approximation and may include effects from explicit deletion.\n- **Memory reclaimed** uses `rate(master_evicted_size_bytes_mem)`; with `offload_on_evict=true`, it is the most useful master-side signal for memory released after the eviction/offload path completes.\n- **File storage net growth** uses `deriv(master_allocated_file_size_bytes)` and is logical occupied-capacity growth, not physical disk write bandwidth.\n- **Client SSD write** is exact `mooncake_ssd_write_bytes_total` throughput when that client metric has been exported into Prometheus. Current Mooncake client metrics may only be printed to logs unless an exporter collects them.\n- If estimated ingress remains above memory reclaimed and allocated memory keeps rising, the offload/eviction path is not keeping up. A rising `PutStart allocation failure` rate confirms user-visible allocation pressure.\n- The Node Exporter row is optional; set the node/device variables if `node_disk_*` metrics are available.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "10.4.0",
      "title": "Reading Guide",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "id": 10,
